# AFD historical membership and lifecycle feasibility

Prepared 14 September for 15 September 2026. Phase: Plan; not launched.

## Question, inputs and unit

Which pre-exposure financing populations and transitions can be reconstructed
without assuming permanent disclosure? Unit: exact AFD financing ID, with a
separate project-parent join. Use the full legacy export (source ID
`afd-full-export` in round-2 manifest), round-3 `afd/` portal tables, country XML,
policy and metadata. Read the round-3 AFD report and profiles. Baseline facts:
3,277 current portal financing IDs; 317 financing/225 project XML IDs in seven
countries; 223/224 legacy records retained. These are observed export counts.

## First test and mandatory challenges

First failing test: CMA123501, missing from current portal/XML, must produce
`lost_visibility` with last-observed information and unknown outcome; it must
not become cancelled or known still unpaid. Second: none of the 193 exact legacy
payment dates may be replaced by an exact minimum XML payment date. Include a
case with missing earlier coverage that must NOT become a first-payment interval.

Locally reconcile all 19 missing IDs listed in `round3/afd/flat-profile.json`,
CTN129703 (missing signature), CZZ276103 (changed signature), all seven legacy
award/signature reversals, and all 13 missing awards in the matched XML set.
Keep original values and join provenance. Assert `value-date` cannot fill missing
awards. Known duplicate parent/component identities cannot substitute for an ID.
All anomaly rows require a disposition, not necessarily a documentary resolution.
For the 12-case sample, use the legacy seven-country financing frame, excluding
these challenge IDs. Publish the exact country-label mapping before selection.

## Routes, budget and stop decisions

Maximum 30 external units, failures included:

1. Up to 12 for publisher transformation/inclusion/retention specifications and
   dated predecessor snapshots: acquired AFD/data.gouv resource identifiers and
   version history first, then official transparency/publication documentation,
   then archive indexes for those exact URLs. A 2024 snapshot cannot alone
   establish pre-JETP membership. An archive crawl timestamp alone is not proof
   of unchanged content or complete portfolio disclosure.
2. Up to 12 for originals: first CMA123501, CTN129703 and CZZ276103; then the
   first two reversal IDs in lexical order; then first missing-award ID; then
   the fixed sample in rank order. Use archived project links and exact financing
   identifiers to seek contract/project fiches or dated decision records. Related
   components are contrary-identity checks, not substitute observations.
3. Reserve 6 for source verification or a discriminating follow-up on these routes.
   Unused earlier allocations may move forward; never take the verification
   reserve for broad discovery. Log allocation changes before the next request.

Stop a route after its listed alternatives fail; no broad financing search.
Without an independently justified historical denominator, incumbent-population
membership is DEFER. Retrospective event and signature-throughput coverage may
still be assessed, conditional on disclosure stability. Signed-only data cannot
support the pending approval-to-signature risk set. Separate loans/grants and
policy/investment; do not infer strata solely from titles.

## Fixed documentary sample

Profile all acquired records locally. For documentary coverage, restrict the
sample frame to AL, MA, IN, SN, ZA, ID, VN at the lender unit below. Partition by
country, DAC energy/non-energy/mixed-or-unmapped, and raw instrument code (missing
is its own value). Sort strata lexicographically, then IDs within each stratum.
Take one ID from each stratum per round, cycling until 12 distinct IDs are chosen
or the frame is exhausted. Save all candidates, ranks and selected flags; no
outcome/date/status filtering or replacement after failed retrieval. Exclude
mandatory challenge IDs from this sample and report them separately. This is a
purposive coverage probe, not an estimate of population document availability.
Report local-document coverage for all 12, and external-attempt coverage with
its own denominator. If the call cap prevents inspecting a selected case, label
it not attempted. Continue first in sample rank order within the assigned budget.

Read and apply `docs/jetp-pilots/2026-09-15/protocol.md` for baseline alternatives,
observation states, source/selection freeze, output schemas and review. That
protocol is part of this assignment, not optional background. Parent trackers:
0735 / GitHub #1345 and 0729 / #1337. No effect estimation or outreach. A DEFER
with precise missing evidence can satisfy every pilot exit criterion.

## Exit criteria

- First acceptance tests fail on naive mappings and pass on the corrected implementation.
- Input hashes, frozen selection and the common units/events/coverage/evidence tables are delivered.
- Every mandatory challenge has an evidenced disposition or a precise unresolved gap.
- Acquisition stays within the cap with failed/not-attempted cases retained.
- Versioned calculations rerun offline from archive paths, with relevant repository gates recorded.
- A separate verification pass reproduces pivotal counts and checks originals.
- Report returns GO/NARROW/DEFER by stage and inputs to the common design matrix.

Outputs: `docs/jetp-pilots/2026-09-15/afd/`; new originals in a separate
`data/jetp/audit-evidence/0737-pilot` DVC bundle. No canonical data changes.

